# Staged by pack.py from reference/bmx.js so the preview ships with a renderer. Generated, not source
# — two copies of a parser in version control is how they drift.
editors/vscode/reference/

# Built by `burxt build render.bx -o bmxrender`, per tools/README.md. A 232K compiled binary that
# rebuilds in seconds does not belong in version control — and a binary is not evidence of the
# source it came from, which this project has written down elsewhere.
tools/bmxrender

# The PNGs live in docs/assets/examples/, which is where the site serves them from. A second copy
# beside the generator is the drift hazard, one directory over.
tools/*.png

# `npm install vscode-textmate vscode-oniguruma` — what the grammar tests need, installed the same way
# CI installs it. Untracked and unignored, it turned up in every `git status` after the first local run
# of `scopes.mjs`.
editors/vscode/node_modules/

# Written by Python the first time anything imports a runner as a module rather than running it —
# `tests/version.py` gets imported to check what its page glob resolves to. Untracked and unignored it
# turns up in every `git status` afterwards, which is the noise `node_modules` above caused and the same
# one-line fix.
#
# **And one was already COMMITTED**, which this line does not undo: `tests/__pycache__/probe.cpython-312.pyc`
# went in with 521f961, the commit that *added* `tests/probe.py` — swept up by a `git add tests/`. It was
# the only tracked `.pyc` in the repository, it is a build artefact of a file already here, and a stale one
# can shadow a source change.
#
# **Ignoring a path has no effect on a path git already tracks, and deleting the file does not stick** —
# any run of `tools/check.sh` imports `probe` and Python writes it straight back, byte-identical, so the
# deletion disappears from `git status` on the next run. Untracking it takes one deliberate command,
# left for whoever commits this rather than staged as a side effect of a cleanup:
#
#     git rm --cached tests/__pycache__/probe.cpython-312.pyc
#
# The rule below is what stops the next one.
tests/__pycache__/

# Andre's golden rules for the Burxt family, kept per-working-copy rather than per-repository, so the
# same file lives in `burxt`, `star-burxt`, `bmx` and `comet-code-playground` without four copies to keep
# in step through git. Also `.claude/` is where a session's own scratch settings land, and those are one
# machine's business.
#
# **Ignored rather than committed on purpose:** the rules are a record of what was learned, and a record
# that travels with the repository invites being read as something the repository enforces. What this
# repository enforces is in `tools/check.sh` and CI, where it can fail.
.claude/
